              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.482,
            0.364,
            0.877,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The figure shown corresponds to the identity"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.56,
            0.407,
            0.799,
            0.428
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_31_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "(a + b)^{2} = a^{2} + 2ab + b^{2}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.483,
            0.436,
            0.672,
            0.456
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you see how?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.541,
            0.883,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Draw figures corresponding to the identities "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(a + b)(a - b) ="
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a^{2}-b^{2}\\mathrm{and}(a+b+c)^{2}=a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2}+2ab+2bc+2ca."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.589,
            0.884,
            0.629
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. An isosceles triangle has perimeter 40 cm; the equal sides are 15 cm each. Find the area of the triangle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.636,
            0.885,
            0.677
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. An isosceles triangle has base 10 cm, and its area is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 \\; \\mathtt { c m } ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . What are the lengths of the equal sides?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.683,
            0.885,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. The area of a right-angled triangle is 54 sq. cm. One of its legs has length 12 cm. Find its perimeter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.73,
            0.886,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. The sides of a triangle are in the ratio 2: 3: 4, and its perimeter is 45 cm. Find its area."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.777,
            0.885,
            0.819
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. The sides of a triangle have lengths 7 cm, 24 cm, 25 cm. Find the area of the triangle in two different ways."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.825,
            0.886,
            0.866
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. If the wheel of a bicycle has a diameter of 60 cm, find how far a cyclist will have travelled after the wheel has rotated 100 times."
